01:17:16,800 --> 01:17:22,800
Marshal Edward "Teddy" Daniels and his partner Chuck, who come to the fictional Shutter Island in Boston Harbor to investigate its
criminal psychiatric facility after one of its patients goes missing; Daniels has his own ulterior motives for taking the case.

15
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
The film stars Leonardo DiCaprio and Mark Ruffalo, with Ben Kingsley,
Max von Sydow and Michelle Williams in supporting roles.

16
01:28:19,199 --> 01:28:25,199
Development began when Phoenix Pictures acquired the film rights to the novel directly from
Lehane after Columbia Pictures had allowed their rights to lapse in 2003.

17
01:33:50,399 --> 01:33:56,399
Phoenix hired Laeta Kalogridis to work on a screenplay for a year, and in 2007
announced that Scorsese and DiCaprio had both joined the project.

18
01:39:21,599 --> 01:39:27,599
Production began on March 6, 2008, at various locations in Massachusetts – Long Island, while not used as a location, was the inspiration for the fictional island –
including Peddocks Island (as the island), East Point (as the lighthouse), and the Medfield State Hospital (as the facility); filming ended on July 2, 2008.

19
01:44:52,800 --> 01:44:58,800
Partnering with Paramount Pictures, the film had its wide release on February
19, 2010, and received generally positive reviews from critics.

20
01:50:24,000 --> 01:50:30,000
It was chosen by the National Board of Review as one of the top ten
films of 2010, and grossed $295 million worldwide.

21
01:55:55,199 --> 01:56:01,199
The film is also noted for its soundtrack, which prominently used classical music, such as that of Gustav
Mahler, Krzysztof Penderecki, György Ligeti, John Cage, Ingram Marshall, and Max Richter.

22
